@startuml
title TH-08 Attack Tree - Order Tampering and Ownership Bypass

skinparam backgroundColor #f4f4f4
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam rectangle {
	BorderColor #5c5c5c
	FontColor #1f1f1f
	RoundCorner 8
}

rectangle "Attacker manipulates order\nintegrity and ownership\n(TH-08)" as ROOT #e6f7ff

rectangle "Attacker tampers request\nparameters during order creation\n(AC-08)" as PARAM_TAMPERING #ffffff
rectangle "Attacker abuses unauthorized\norder state transitions\n(AC-16)" as STATE_ABUSE #ffffff
rectangle "Attacker exploits checkout\nconcurrency/race conditions\n(AC-15)" as RACE_ABUSE #ffffff

rectangle "Mitigate with server-side input\nvalidation and RBAC ownership checks\nControls: IV-001, AC-004\nTests: ST-015\nReq: RF-14, RF-20" as M_PARAM_TAMPERING #d6f5ea
rectangle "Mitigate with strict authorization\non cancel/finalize operations\nControls: AC-004\nTests: ST-015\nReq: RF-20" as M_STATE_ABUSE #d6f5ea
rectangle "Mitigate with idempotency and\ntransaction monitoring controls\nControls: IV-001, LM-002\nTests: ST-015" as M_RACE_ABUSE #d6f5ea

ROOT -down-> PARAM_TAMPERING
ROOT -down-> STATE_ABUSE
ROOT -down-> RACE_ABUSE

PARAM_TAMPERING -down-> M_PARAM_TAMPERING
STATE_ABUSE -down-> M_STATE_ABUSE
RACE_ABUSE -down-> M_RACE_ABUSE

note bottom
Attack path logic:
- Branches from ROOT are OR alternatives.
- Each mitigation block defines the primary defensive response for that branch.
end note

@enduml
